<content>
  <section><para>A streaming service offers two options for subscription plans. Option A charges $10.99 a month plus $2 per movie. Option B charges $5.99 a month plus $3 per movie. The table below describes this. Which of the following systems of equations represents the two options for one month?</para>
<table class="os-raise-doubleheadertable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">\(x\) (Number of movies</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">0</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">1</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">2</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">3</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Option A</entry>
      <entry>10.99</entry>
      <entry>12.99</entry>
      <entry>14.99</entry>
      <entry>16.99</entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">Option B</entry>
      <entry>5.99</entry>
      <entry>8.99</entry>
      <entry>11.99</entry>
      <entry>14.99</entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>
<br/></section>
</content>
